<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<component type="desktop-application">
  <id>online.fujinet.go.sms.gnome</id>
  <metadata_license>CC0-1.0</metadata_license>
  <project_license>GPL-3.0-or-later</project_license>
  <name>FujiNet Go SMS</name>
  <summary>A Sega Master System with a built-in FujiNet</summary>
  <description>
    <p>
      A self-contained Sega Master System with a FujiNet built in: browse a
      network host from the console, boot games over the network, and let a
      FujiNet program keep talking to the network, all in one application.
    </p>
    <p>
      FujiNet's CONFIG program is built in and starts at power-on, exactly as
      on the FujiNet Master System cartridge. Local .sms and .sg cartridge
      images can be opened in its place, or imported to FujiNet's SD folder
      with Import Cartridge to SD and booted from CONFIG. Soft Reset restarts
      whatever is running, and Reset to CONFIG ejects the cartridge and brings
      CONFIG back.
    </p>
    <p>
      Six consoles are built in: the Master System and the Master System II,
      each in NTSC and PAL, the Japanese Master System with its YM2413 FM
      sound, and the Mark III with the optional FM Sound Unit. The emulator is
      MAME's Master System transposed to C, with the FujiNet cartridge running
      the real cartridge firmware's own protocol and mapper sources, so it
      behaves as the hardware does.
    </p>
    <p>
      Gamepads are picked up as they are plugged in and out, and every control
      can be remapped to a key or a gamepad button. A native debugger has a
      command prompt, the Z80 and console RAM, disassembly with breakpoints,
      the VDP with its name table, tile, sprite and palette views, the sound
      chips and I/O ports, and the FujiNet cartridge.
    </p>
    <p>
      No BIOS is required and nothing copyrighted is included: every console
      boots the cartridge directly, and the only built-in program is
      FujiNet's own CONFIG client. Importing a BIOS of your own is optional.
    </p>
  </description>
  <launchable type="desktop-id">online.fujinet.go.sms.gnome.desktop</launchable>
  <url type="homepage">https://fujinet.online/</url>
  <url type="bugtracker">https://github.com/FujiNetWIFI/fujinet-go-sms-desktop/issues</url>
  <url type="vcs-browser">https://github.com/FujiNetWIFI/fujinet-go-sms-desktop</url>
  <developer id="online.fujinet">
    <name>Thomas Cherryhomes</name>
  </developer>
  <content_rating type="oars-1.1"/>
